{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## RCA — confirmed root cause, proof, and defect origin\n\n### Mechanism (proven at runtime, twice, independently)\n\n`_hash_basis(..., at_current_gate_ref=True)` (`src/rebar/llm/plan_review/manifest.py:246-260`)\ncatches `Exception` around the gate-ref resolution, logs a WARNING, and returns the in-place\nworking tree as the hashing basis. Its only production caller is the claim-gate freshness\nre-check (`src/rebar/llm/plan_review/attest.py:605-613`, inside `compute_validity` for\n`kind == plan-review`).\n\n### Discriminating experiment (E1)\n\nOne signed attested attestation pinning `dep.py`; the dependency drifts and LANDS on\n`origin/main`; the working tree is rolled back to the reviewed bytes. Varying ONLY whether the\ngate ref resolves:\n\n```\ngate ref resolvable   -> {'ok': False, 'verdict': 'stale-code'}   claim BLOCKED\ngate ref UNRESOLVABLE -> {'ok': True,  'verdict': 'certified'}    claim ALLOWED\n```\n\nRun independently twice (orchestrator + a blind investigator) with the same result. This kills\nthe docstring's own justification — \"the conservative direction, since the checkout normally\ncontains the drift\" — because the degradation is demonstrably the PERMISSIVE direction whenever\nthe checkout does not contain the drift.\n\n### Violated authority (legitimacy = defect)\n\n* `docs/plan-review-gate.md:1567` — `| Claim gate | **fail-closed** | a missing/stale\n  plan-review attestation BLOCKS the claim |`; `:1574` \"reserve fail-closed for the claim gate\".\n* `docs/repo-snapshot-gates.md` — \"attested **fails closed** — it never serves the wrong tree\";\n  itemizing \"the gate does **not** fall back to some other tree\".\n* `docs/adr/0002-code-drift-invalidation.md:46` — \"keeping the fallback fail-closed\".\n* `docs/plan-review-gate.md:939` (operator ruling 39f8-ae7c) — \"it never silently resolves the\n  gate to its default\".\n\nThe premise the authorization rests on is false in both environments where the fallback fires:\nthe review-bot's clone holds a PATCHSET, and the deployed MCP box's `/var/gerrit/site/mcp-code`\nworking tree is pinned at container-boot clone time (`infra/scripts/mcp-entrypoint.sh`,\n`git clone --filter=blob:none --single-branch --branch main`) with NO subsequent\n`git fetch`/`pull` of the tree, while `refs/remotes/origin/main` does advance. That checkout is\nsystematically BEHIND main — it lacks the drift rather than containing it.\n\n### Blast radius\n\n* **Review-bot (the messenger).** `clone_change_ref` does `git init` + `git fetch <url>\n  <patchset-ref>` with no `origin` remote, so the fallback fires on 100% of runs. Its consumer\n  is `bugfix_size_gate.classify_plan_review_attestation`, whose\n  `ACCEPTED_VERDICTS = {certified, stale-code, stale-head}` absorbs both outcomes. **The\n  observed log line has no verdict consequence.** The review-bot surfaced the defect; it is\n  not the victim.\n* **Claim gate (the victim).** `verify.require_plan_review_for_claim = true`. On the box the ref\n  itself resolves, but the same broad `except` also swallows `_cache.acquire` failures —\n  `repo_snapshot._ensure_blobs_present` is explicitly \"BEST-EFFORT and silent on failure\" on a\n  blobless clone, so a failed blob top-up degrades to that stale boot-time tree.\n  *Labelled: verified by code reading, not reproduced on the box.*\n* **Signing side unaffected.** `dependency_hashes` / `_rehash` take the no-flag branch\n  (`current_code_root()`), so **no signed attestation's `verified_at_sha` or manifest hashes\n  were ever computed on a substituted basis.** `verified_at_sha` pins the SIGNING basis only;\n  nothing records the VERIFY basis — which is why the substitution is undetectable.\n\n### Visibility (why \"silent\" is the anomaly)\n\n`compute_validity` -> `{valid, reason, verdict}` (+ `health`, `registry_drift`);\n`claim_gate_check` -> `{ok, reason, verdict}`. **No basis field, no sidecar, no telemetry.**\nThe single trace is one `logger.warning`. This is out of step with the codebase's own\nconventions: `bugfix_size_gate`'s `infra`/abstain bucket, `registry_drift` surfaced on\n`compute_validity`'s own result (ADR 0053), `_UNPINNED` (\"honest and fail-closed\"),\n`stale-store`, the close gate's `unavailable` + structured event, and the DET floor's recorded\nabstention. Tightest comparison: **inside `claim_gate_check` itself**, an unavailable *signing\nsubsystem* fails closed with `verdict: \"error\"`, while an unavailable *basis* degrades silently.\n\n### Defect origin — `caused_by` 72d9-8fbd-3a9e-48a6 (athletic-esthetical-polecat)\n\nIntroducing commit **`2e2fe3f7d25c`** (2026-07-24, trailer\n`rebar-ticket: 72d9-8fbd-3a9e-48a6`). Established with `git log -L218,262:…manifest.py -w -C -M`;\n`a9aed66ce412` in the same range is a Ruff-hygiene no-op and was walked through as a carrier.\n\n**Divergence from what a whole-file blame would say, recorded per protocol.** The broad-except\ndegrade itself is OLDER — `b25fafcd188b` (2026-06-27, epic `raze-vet-ditch` story\n`e308-daf0-d765-40d3` / `piney-gold-day`) — so a naive blame attributes there. That is wrong:\nunder `b25fafcd188b` the drift check was the tautology 72d9 exists to fix, so the degrade could\nnot flip any verdict. `2e2fe3f7d25c` made the check consequential AND repointed it from a pinned\nSHA to `origin/main`, creating the obligation \"every claim environment must resolve\n`origin/main`\" while carrying the now-consequential degrade forward unreconciled against the\ndocumented fail-closed posture. Unmet obligation, hence `close_class=regression`.\n\nThe review-bot's consumption (`1920dc9fe559`, 2026-08-03) only made the condition visible in\nlogs; it post-dates 72d9 and did not create it.\n\n### Two gaps the repair must respect\n\n1. The existing pin `test_ref_coherence.py::test_hash_basis_resolution` asserts only the fallback\n   *path* and *does not crash* — never a resulting VERDICT. The suite was structurally blind to\n   this flip, so the RED oracle must be verdict-level.\n2. `source=local` stays exempt: there the working tree is the correct, documented back-out, not a\n   substitution. Only the attested-but-unresolvable arm is defective.\n"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787961012735245057,"uuid":"0308461f-cee2-4fd6-a2a3-0a8b6f5c29e7"}